Attributes

.are special words used within the opening tag of an HTML element 
.provide additional info about HTML elements 
.used to configure and adjust the element's behavior, appearance, or functionality 
    .tell the browser how to render the element/ how it should behave during interactions 
.formatted as name="value"
.comprises:
    .name  - specifies the kind of additional info or property getting defined for the element 
    .value - value assigned to define the specific setting/ behavior 
            .always placed in quotes  


Types
.classified based on their function and the type of elements they modify

    .class - groups elements and allows styling 
    .style - inline CSS styles
    .src - specifies the source of various resources 
    .contenteditable - determines whether the content within the element is editable 
    .role - specifies the element's accessibility role 
    .tabindex - determines the order of focus during keyboard navigation
    .id - assigns a unique identifier to an element, allowing targeting with CSS or JS
    .alt - provides alternative text for images, essential for accessibility and SEO
    .title - creates a tooltip that appears whrn a user hovers over the element
    .lang - specifies the language of the element's content, aiding with translation and accessibility 


    Other attributes 
    .event - define the actions to be taken on specific browser events 
    .input - specific to input elements within <form> tags
    .image - specific to the <img> element for handling images 
    .link - specific to linking elements like <a> and <link>
    .table - used with table elements like <table>, <th>, <tr>, and <td>
    .style - define styles directly on an element 
    .media - related to media elements like <audio> and <video>
    .accessibility - help improve accessibility, such as alt for images and aria-* attributes 
    .meta - used with meta elements to specify metadata like charset

Pointers
.lowercase attributes - for consistency and better readability
.quote them - to avoid errors e.g where the value contains spaces or special characters
.consistency when quoting values throughout the document 
.booleans don't require values; if present, its considered present 
.ideal order when present:
    id > class > other global attributes > specific attributes > event attributes 